# Kubeflow Trainer

## Role

`TrainerClient` (`api/trainer_client.py`) is a thin facade. All execution logic lives in `backends/`.
Backend is selected at construction via `KubernetesBackendConfig`, `ContainerBackendConfig`, or
`LocalProcessBackendConfig`.

## Package map

| Path | Responsibility |
|------|----------------|
| `api/` | Public `TrainerClient` — no backend-specific branching |
| `backends/base.py` | `RuntimeBackend` ABC — contract for all backends |
| `backends/kubernetes/` | TrainJob CR creation (production path) |
| `backends/container/` | Docker/Podman local execution |
| `backends/localprocess/` | Host subprocess smoke tests |
| `options/` | Callable options mutating `job_spec` in `train()` |
| `types/types.py` | Shared schemas (`TrainJob`, `Runtime`, trainers) |

## Invariants

- Cross-component import boundaries are enforced by `make lint-imports` (see `.importlinter`).
- Never add backend-specific job creation in `TrainerClient`; extend `RuntimeBackend` + config instead.
- Kubernetes options must guard with `isinstance(backend, KubernetesBackend)` in `__call__`.
- Local backends (`container`, `localprocess`) support `CustomTrainer` only.
- Backends return shared status vocabulary: `Created`, `Running`, `Complete`, `Failed`.

## Common changes

- New K8s option → `options/kubernetes.py` + `kubernetes_test.py` (see `references/common-changes.md`)
- Extend backend → `backends/<name>/backend.py` + co-located `*_test.py`
- New trainer type → `types/types.py` + exports in `types/__init__.py`

## Pitfalls

- `LocalProcessBackend.train()` accepts `initializer` but ignores it today.
- `ContainerBackend` v1: `CustomTrainer` only; serializes `func` into container command.
- Do not import `kubeflow.spark` or `kubeflow.optimizer` from trainer code.

## Verify

```bash
uv run pytest -q kubeflow/trainer/backends/kubernetes/backend_test.py
uv run ruff check kubeflow/trainer/path/to/file.py
```

